   "evidence": "The probe seeded a durable unfinished attempt and simulated both restart sequences. At HEAD, reconciliation executes `state.attempt = null` and judges failure using `d.bootSha !== attempt.sha`, without consulting job status. The existing deploy path calls `waitForHealthy` after restarting and can subsequently restore and restart the previous release (service.ts:633-653). The reconciliation module is absent at base. Actual launchd restart and rollback were not exercised."
  },
  "B": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "Suppose the daemon restarts on the old version while the deploy job is still running its 8\u201345 minutes of checks and drain. The deploy is then recorded as failed and automatic deploys are blocked, even though the job goes on to succeed. The opposite also happens: the new version boots, the record is cleared, and then the job's health check fails and rolls back. In that case the rolled-back daemon records no failure and no feed item, so the failed deploy goes unreported.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun test $TMPDIR/adjud-651/f1.test.ts $TMPDIR/adjud-651/f1b.test.ts (persisted attempt for NEW; tick AutoDeploy with bootSha=NEW then OLD; separately tick with bootSha=OLD while the job is still running)",
    "output": "f1: after new boot: {\"handled\":1,\"attempt\":null,\"blocked\":null}; after rollback boot: {\"handled\":1,\"attempt\":null,\"blocked\":null} (no block, no feed). f1b: state: {...\"blocked\":{\"sha\":\"bbbb\u2026\",\"reason\":\"Deploy of bbbb\u2026 did not restart successfully; running aaaa\u2026\"}} although the job has not finished"
